s CI broadly as any information disclosed by any means — no express identification requirement. Contradiction, evidence [23].\n\n- nda-19 (Survival of obligations): [29] \"Agreement shall remain in force in perpetuity\" — obligations survive. Entailment, evidence [29].\n\n- nda-12 (Permissible development of similar information): Not mentioned. NotMentioned.\n\n- nda-20 (Permissible post-agreement possession): Not mentioned. NotMentioned.\n\n- nda-3 (Inclusion of verbally conveyed information): [23] \"disclosed whether in writing, orally or by any other means.\" Entailment, evidence [23].\n\n- nda-18 (No solicitation): [27] \"I will not attempt to contact the employees, customers, creditors, suppliers or landlords of any client\" — non-solicitation/non-contact of representatives. Entailment, evidence [27].\n\n- nda-7 (Sharing with third-parties): [25] \"not disclose it to any third party without the prior written consent of The Business Partnership\" — sharing permitted with consent. Entailment, evidence [25].\n\n- nda-17 (Permissible copy): [25] says \"make no copies thereof\" (absolute), but [34] says \"must not be copied... without the consent of TBP\" — implying copying with consent is allowed. The [34] clause provides a circumstance where copying is permissible. Entailment, evidence [34]. Hmm, but [25] contradicts. Given [34] explicitly conditions copying on consent, I'll go Entailment with [34].\n\n- nda-8 (Notice on compelled disclosure): Not mentioned. NotMentioned.\n\n- nda-13 (Permissible acquirement of similar information): Not mentioned. NotMentioned.\n\n- nda-5 (Sharing with employees): Not mentioned (no clause about sharing with Receiving Party's employees). NotMentioned.\n\n- nda-4 (Limited use): [25] \"use it solely for the purpose as agreed between parties.\" Entailment, evidence [25].\n\nAction: human_feedback {\"nda_id\": \"nda-17\", \"evidence_ids\": [34]}",
